{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see","id":73035,"title":"What Pantheon would you like to see?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-15T22:58:58-08:00","id":73035,"title":"What Pantheon would you like to see?","content":"So as Scion Origin is being made I was wondering if people would share what Panteons they would like to see in the game. (You could probably avoid the main ones like Greek/Roman Egyptian, Norse Tuatha etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T00:34:22-08:00","id":73072,"title":"","content":"I'm currently writing for Scion 1\u00b0, a pantheon for the Wicca, the neo-paganism. But I've stopped since the new Scion is coming, I'd rather wait for new rules to do that. It's an emerging duotheism religion which the God and the Goddess have different roles to play. They could split into different Gods...<br /> The most important pantheons should be the Hindu one, the Chinese one (even if it's somehow related...), the ones that still &quot;exist&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T05:31:17-08:00","id":73139,"title":"","content":"I've become a huge fan of Mesopotamian mythology lately, so I'd love to see the Annuna in Hero. They're the oldest recorded religion in human history, you can see elements of their religion in the myths of several other Mediterranean mythologies, and their Gods and stories are just really cool. I said in another thread: I'll understand if they're not in Hero, but if Demigod and God really DO get to include more Pantheons, then the Annuna deserve to be one of the first Pantheons to be considered for inclusion. Failing that? They deserve to be in a Pantheon-expansion book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T05:41:08-08:00","id":73141,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see more non-european and pre-roman european pantheons, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T05:50:29-08:00","id":73142,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to see the Gaulish Pantheon being officially canon. La Biblioth\u00e8que Interdite have done a good job with it, but it was still a little underwhelming. And since they closed down and we certainly won't have Scion 2\u00b0 published in France, I can't really count on the french fan-base for a rewrite (Scion doesn't have a good rep here). And come on, Cernunnos and druids are awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T12:37:31-08:00","id":73304,"title":"","content":"I second the motion for Annuna as a new base pantheon. I Figured they'd just clean up all the previous official pantheon writeups (Yazata, Shen, Tuatha) and add them in with the ones from Scion: Hero.<br /> Actually I'd like them to add the Atua (Polynesians) as well, since they are actually still active (just ask anyone from Hawaii about Madame Pele).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T14:28:16-08:00","id":73376,"title":"","content":"So many to choose from\u2026 I don\u2019t think I could pick just one. Check out <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">John\u2019s Scion Resources</a>, especially the Pantheons and Downloads; and be sure to look at the map to get a sense of what the possibilities are. Of the ones discussed there, I\u2019d also likely favor the Annuna; of the ones on the map but not (yet) addressed, I\u2019d probably want either the Australian Aboriginals or the Algonquin of North America. <br /> <br /> In the latter case, I\u2019d be sure to emphasize that they\u2019re no more a generic \u201cNative Americans\u201d Pantheon than the Amatsukami are a generic \u201cPantheon of the Orient\u201d: e.g., name-drop a couple of their North American neighbors when describing their relations with other Pantheons. (Likewise, I\u2019d expect the Australian Aboriginals to name-drop one or two neighboring Pantheons that would be slated for development some time later, such as the Phillipino Pantheon and/or the various Pantheons of Southeast Asia. Heck, I\u2019d want <i>every</i> Pantheon statted up to mention at least one Pantheon that <i>hasn\u2019t</i> been statted up and that isn\u2019t mentioned by any other Pantheon; there are enough of them that doing so is feasible for <i>at least</i> the first round of Pantheons.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T14:59:42-08:00","id":73406,"title":"","content":"I have many pantheons on my list, but of the pantheons not covered in first edition, the Inca Pantheon tops my list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T15:30:24-08:00","id":73418,"title":"","content":"Hmm..&quot;Pantheon&quot; revolves around geo-cultural centers...I confess I have other ideas that I'd think are &quot;pre-cultural.&quot; But I concede that such may not be suitable to what is wanted here...so...<br /> <br /> *bows out*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T17:49:36-08:00","id":73471,"title":"","content":"I hope the Gaulish pantheon is not in the new material. Those guys did a great job, but there are pantheons out there that have actual mythologies that need to come way before the Gauls about whom we really know nothing. Any North American pantheon other than the Aztec please, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T17:53:07-08:00","id":73473,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see one of the Indigenous Australian pantheons get a look in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T18:11:45-08:00","id":73484,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73471#post73471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the Gaulish pantheon is not in the new material. Those guys did a great job, but there are pantheons out there that have actual mythologies that need to come way before the Gauls about whom we really know nothing. Any North American pantheon other than the Aztec please, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods* I understand that about the Gaul. I'm a little skeptical about any North American pantheon however.<br /> <br /> I'm more onboard with the Sumerian pantheon.<br /> And I admit, I found JSR's Arabian pantheon a good read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T19:39:51-08:00","id":73511,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Polynesian/Maori</li> <li>Central Africa or some sort</li> <li>Slavic</li> <li>Finnish</li> <li>North American (don't try to make a pan-cultural one. Pick a particular mythology and stick with it)</li> <li>Pre-Islam Arabian</li> <li>Babylonian</li> </ol><br /> I don't expect all of these to be included, but if any of them were I'd be pretty stoked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T19:43:54-08:00","id":73513,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a Native American Pantheon as well as a Pantheon made from the idea behind many myths but more nebulous in identity, like Sun Father, Wanderer, Monster Slayer, Storm Lord, Architect, Crippled Warrior, Marksman, Psychopomp, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T21:28:54-08:00","id":73543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73484#post73484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *nods* I understand that about the Gaul. I'm a little skeptical about any North American pantheon however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve already seen two that work reasonably well (the Aztecs and JSR\u2019s Inuits); so I don\u2019t see why there couldn\u2019t be others based on other North American cultures. I\u2019ve already mentioned the Algonquin (IIRC, that\u2019s the culture whence came Pocahontas); there are literally a half dozen others with rich enough polytheistic traditions to support full-on Pantheons of their own: e.g., the Hopi, Iroquois, Blackfoots (\u201cBlack<i>feet</i>!\u201d), Cherokee, Navajo, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73484#post73484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more onboard with the Sumerian pantheon.<br /> And I admit, I found JSR's Arabian pantheon a good read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, the Arabian Pantheon is just as sketchy in terms of real-world research as the Gaulish Pantheon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aermas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73513#post73513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see a Native American Pantheon as well as a Pantheon made from the idea behind many myths but more nebulous in identity, like Sun Father, Wanderer, Monster Slayer, Storm Lord, Architect, Crippled Warrior, Marksman, Psychopomp, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by \u201cNative American Pantheon\u201d you mean a multicultural melting pot of various Native American religions, no thanks. Ditto to a Jungian \u201cPantheon of Archetypes\u201d. I didn\u2019t like the homogenizing when they did it with the Allied Pantheon, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-17-2014, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T05:45:13-08:00","id":73673,"title":"","content":"k...I think I need to make another attempt at Native America's Great Spirits.<br /> In the appropriate thread of course.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T08:26:13-08:00","id":73731,"title":"","content":"I my mind, the panth\u00e9ons must cover the earth.<br /> <br /> So 3 pantheons for Europe : Nordic, Greco-Roman, Gaullish<br /> 3 panth\u00e9ons for America : Aztec, North america native of choice, Vodoo (i prefer Inca to vodoo, but since it was in the base book of previous edition)<br /> 3 panth\u00e9ons for Asia : Japan, Chinese, Hindu<br /> 1 pantheon for Africa : Egyptian (because we have less choice here of panth\u00e9ons well known).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2307-arcanum-magicae","name":"Arcanum Magicae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T09:22:16-08:00","id":73748,"title":"","content":"We're getting the Orisha, which is awesome. Anyways, what I want is an Ugarit (Caananite) pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T09:29:24-08:00","id":73753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Magicae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73731#post73731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I my mind, the panth\u00e9ons must cover the earth.<br /> <br /> So 3 pantheons for Europe : Nordic, Greco-Roman, Gaullish<br /> 3 panth\u00e9ons for America : Aztec, North america native of choice, Vodoo (i prefer Inca to vodoo, but since it was in the base book of previous edition)<br /> 3 panth\u00e9ons for Asia : Japan, Chinese, Hindu<br /> 1 pantheon for Africa : Egyptian (because we have less choice here of panth\u00e9ons well known).</div> </div> </div> </div>South America and Australia weep tears of loneliness =(<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T09:48:24-08:00","id":73763,"title":"","content":"So, I'd really like to so several separate Native American pantheons, I don't personally know much about them, but I feel like they deserve some representation, and I think they'd be interesting.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd really like to see as some sort of side supplemental (hell even as an April fools joke pdf as long as it got a decent treatment) detailing the Cthulhu Mythos Great Old Ones as a third faction, and rules for scions of the Crawling Chaos and the Black Goat of the Woods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T10:04:32-08:00","id":73773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73748#post73748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're getting the Orisha, which is awesome. Anyways, what I want is an Ugarit (Caananite) pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, do we have confirmation that we're getting <i>Orisha</i> rather than <i>Loa</i>? Because the two terms aren't interchangeable. Or - be still my beating heart - dare we hope for <i>both?!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T12:53:26-08:00","id":73840,"title":"","content":"Actually most of the gods in the Loa were just renames and syncretizations of the original Orishas, they'll probably just revert them back to what they were back in Africa, which I'm all for anyway.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of pantheons covering the earth, it gives us a better spread that way. Since people have done fan-writeups consisting of North American conglomerate pantheons, all the OP writers need to do is break them back apart and do some more research and we'll get at least 5 more pantheons out of it. South America has the Inca, Maya, Zapotec, and Toltec to expand into other pantheons, so there's that continent. <br /> <br /> Who gets Indonesia? That's a lot of area that doesn;t get much mention either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T14:18:17-08:00","id":73877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73543#post73543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If by \u201cNative American Pantheon\u201d you mean a multicultural melting pot of various Native American religions, no thanks. Ditto to a Jungian \u201cPantheon of Archetypes\u201d. I didn\u2019t like the homogenizing when they did it with the Allied Pantheon, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I would like at least one of the many to choose from; Navajo or Cherokee, or better yet both<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I'd kind of like a Pantheon of Titans. I'd love to play a Scion whose progenitor is Prometheus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T15:31:09-08:00","id":73913,"title":"","content":"for a Native American pantheon, I'd much rather see something from the pacific northwest--Salish or Haida, for example. Think of the awesome art that could be included in a section on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T16:40:59-08:00","id":73953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Magicae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73731#post73731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I my mind, the panth\u00e9ons must cover the earth.<br /> <br /> So 3 pantheons for Europe : Nordic, Greco-Roman, Gaullish<br /> 3 panth\u00e9ons for America : Aztec, North america native of choice, Vodoo (i prefer Inca to vodoo, but since it was in the base book of previous edition)<br /> 3 panth\u00e9ons for Asia : Japan, Chinese, Hindu<br /> 1 pantheon for Africa : Egyptian (because we have less choice here of panth\u00e9ons well known).</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do not normally site the &quot;Detritus of All Knowledge&quot; (ie: Wikipedia) as a viable &quot;source,&quot; a simple search thru it reveals the following: (<i>Confirmed by the dozen or so thick mythology books in my copious library)</i><br /> <br /> West Africa:<br /> - Akan of the people of Ghana &amp; Ivory Coast<br /> - Dahomey (Fon) of the Denin Nation<br /> - Efik of Nigeria &amp; Cameroon<br /> - Odinani of the Igbo people (Nigeria &amp; Cameroon<br /> - Serer (Senegal and Gambia)<br /> - Yoruba (Nigeria and Benin)<br /> <br /> And the above is just the prominent West African Religions...there more in West Africa, and many, many more throughout Africa Herself. It would be easy to do...the hard part would be which Pantheons to choose. I for one would like to see a respectfully done series of Pantheons based off of Real World ones from Africa. Not cobbled together ones from various mashups. Africa has so much to offer, from Her People to Her Culture.<br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T21:59:40-08:00","id":74113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73913#post73913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for a Native American pantheon, I'd much rather see something from the pacific northwest--Salish or Haida, for example. Think of the awesome art that could be included in a section on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, Coyote is a very tempting God as well as the Monsterslaying Twins, &amp; skinwalkers would be awesome enemies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T23:02:04-08:00","id":74137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aermas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=74113#post74113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, Coyote is a very tempting God as well as the Monsterslaying Twins, &amp; skinwalkers would be awesome enemies</div> </div> </div> </div>Raven &gt; Coyote. That is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T00:18:49-08:00","id":74149,"title":"","content":"This is why I forsee a long line of Pantheon-specific supplements for Scion 2e: we\u2019re going to start out with ten Pantheons in Hero, plus a few more in each of Demigod and God; but that only scratches the surface of what\u2019s possible. <br /> <br /> For North America, I\u2019d like to see at least four Pantheons early on: the Aztecs, the Inuits, something from east of the Mississippi in the U.S., amd something from the American West. Make the latter two as unlike each other as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T03:58:55-08:00","id":74189,"title":"","content":"- Inca.<br /> - Maya<br /> - Welsh.<br /> - Yoruba<br /> - Persian<br /> - Arabian<br /> - China<br /> - Filipines<br /> - Russia<br /> - Massai<br /> - Zulo <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_gt-baf-table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_gt-baf-table_td\"></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T05:13:15-08:00","id":74208,"title":"","content":"Pacific Northwest it's Raven not Coyote that's the trickster...?<br /> <br /> Hey...*gives them the squinty eye* Hmm...shapeshifters..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T05:20:34-08:00","id":74211,"title":"","content":"My big ones are likely to be core anyway, Greek, Norse, and Chinese. As far as less likely, Mesopotamian does sound really attractive as it's hard to come up with pantheons that are actually older and the earliest gods make for some interesting history, also Gilgamesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T06:38:01-08:00","id":74235,"title":"","content":"Just to keep track here...since that thread on Native Americans went away...<br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Pueblo Southwest</b> (Hopi, Zuni, ); Kokopelli; Sio Humis; Muyingwa; Tokpela; Taiowa; Sotuknang; Poqanghoya and Palongawhoya; Coyote; Kerwan and Katchina Mana; Spider Man and Spider Woman; Ahul<br /> Adds from <b>Navajo</b>; Yolkai Estasan; Estanatlehi; Hastseltsi<br /> <br /> <b>Iroquios</b>; Onatha; Ya-o-gah; Adekagagwaa; Ga-oh; Hahgwehdiyu; Hahgwehdaetgan; Atahensic; Yoskeha; Hino; Ha Wen Neyu; Neoga; Tarhuhyiawahku; Ioskeha; Dajoji; Gohone<br /> Wabanaki/Abenaki; Gluskab; Tabaldak; Malsumis; See-gwen; Nee-ben; Pe-ben; Mat-gwas; A-gaskw; Kee-zos-en; Moos-bas; Pomola; Pla-ween-noo; Nanom-keea-po-da; Ask-wee-da-eed; Wad-zoos-en; Tsi-noo; Wa-won-dee-a-megw<br /> <br /> <b>Pawnee</b>; Uti Hiata; Pah; Basket Woman; Flint Man; Shakuru; nahurak(Pahuk, Nakiskat, Tsurapako, Kitsawitsak, and Pahua); Atira; Tirawa<br /> <br /> <b>Sioux/Lakota</b>; Haokah; Skan; Iya; Wakan Tanka; Ictinike; Whope (&quot;Falling Star&quot; aka Ptehehincalasanwin or &quot;White Buffalo Calf Woman&quot;): Wi; Anog Ite; Tate; Ta Tanka; Capa; Iktomi; Cetan<br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> Obviously not complete at all...Still trying something...work in progress and all that. Something to wrap my mind around since...it still kinda bothers me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T09:28:48-08:00","id":74316,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm hoping for the Korean and Maori pantheons the most, but other than that, I'd also like to see the Yoruban, Inuit, Haida, Incan, Mesopotamian, Finnish, Slavic, Welsh, Tibetan, Mongolian, Indonesian and Aboriginal Australian pantheons.<br /> <br /> ...I'm not going to get every pantheon I want, am I?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/990-maplesamurai","name":"MapleSamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T09:41:10-08:00","id":74328,"title":"","content":"Brasilian Tupi and Paraguayan Guarani.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:41:34-08:00","id":74419,"title":"","content":"I definitely want more pantheons rather than less, though I'm willing to concede that some of them would probably have to appear in later books. Here's my list for what I'd like to see in the first book:<br /> <br /> Sumerian<br /> Egyptian<br /> Greek<br /> Norse<br /> Chinese<br /> Indian<br /> At least one sub-Saharan African pantheon (not sure which would work best)<br /> Aztec<br /> One more American pantheon, either Inca or something from North America.<br /> <br /> In later books, I'd definitely want to see the following:<br /> <br /> Irish<br /> Polynesian<br /> Persian<br /> Japanese<br /> Voodoo<br /> Slavic<br /> Either Inca or another North American pantheon<br /> A non-Inca South American pantheon, if we have enough data for one.<br /> Yet another sub-Saharan African pantheon<br /> A Mongol/Turkic pantheon<br /> A North African/Berber pantheon is there's enough data for one.<br /> Gaulish<br /> Pre-Islamic Arabic<br /> Korean<br /> <br /> My big concern is to make sure major population centers are covered with a pantheon. Right now, Eastern Europe and Central Asian are pretty bereft of possibility, as is Africa. The Americas are also pretty barren- I don't want all my South American Scions to need to be descended from European pantheons, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/794-el-pinko-grande","name":"el pinko grande","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:42:37-08:00","id":74420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=73840#post73840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually most of the gods in the Loa were just renames and syncretizations of the original Orishas, they'll probably just revert them back to what they were back in Africa, which I'm all for anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really - they're a mishmash of Yoruba, Igbo and Ashanti gods mostly, but with a hefty dose of Catholicism. They are drawn from Yoruba mroe than others, sure but Yoruba get really irritated with the conflation of the two religions as 'basically the same thing'.<br /> (Personally I'm not Yoruba, I'm Esan, but this is coming from Yoruba theologians and practitioners I know)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T12:34:25-08:00","id":74464,"title":"","content":"I find the syncretism in <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syncretism#Other_modern_syncretic_religions\" target=\"_blank\">Voodoo</a> kind of fascinating...but annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T14:40:19-08:00","id":74567,"title":"","content":"&quot;South America has the Inca, Maya, Zapotec, and Toltec to expand into other pantheons, so there's that continent.&quot;<br /> <br /> Except Central America is a geological and geographic part of North America. Central and South America's association has more to do with being colonized by Spain. Which has little to do with the myths, legends and pantheons extant BEFORE the colonization/genocide. So, from that list, you're left with Inca.<br /> <br /> P.S. Good luck with distinguishing Zapotec and Toltec as well. See my post on the Gaulish gods for the problem with Toltec mythology. It's THERE. But there's not that much we can get to, comparatively speaking. The Zapotec bring up the same issues as trying to differentiate between the Roman and Greek pantheons. Yup, there are differences. Are there ENOUGH differences to make dividing them worthwhile.<br /> <br /> Same thing for the Inca as well. There is also Moche, Chimor, etc. But is there ENOUGH on either to come up with a viable pantheon without just making up the myths from essentially whole cloth.<br /> <br /> I am a professional archaeologist and it's just not that easy to jump from an artifact, even if it's obviously religious, obviously depicts a deity who is obviously doing something that's a part of his/her myth and say &quot;We know who this god is and what they're doing.&quot; It's essentially a level of make-believe that I would prefer to avoid when there is SO MUCH mythology out there that is rich, vibrant and accessible. Let's do that stuff first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 02-18-2014, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T15:45:51-08:00","id":74606,"title":"","content":"\u200bSouth America would Inca, Aymara, Patagonean, Tupi, Guarani and Tamaio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T19:19:30-08:00","id":74726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>el pinko grande</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=74419#post74419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My big concern is to make sure major population centers are covered with a pantheon. Right now, Eastern Europe and Central Asian are pretty bereft of possibility, as is Africa. The Americas are also pretty barren- I don't want all my South American Scions to need to be descended from European pantheons, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Although it brings up an interesting question: where will the default Scion settings focus their attention? Traditionally, White Wolf has focused on the people inhabiting North America in general, and the United States in particular; given the nation\u2019s \u201cmelting pot\u201d nature, that leaves a lot of room to justify the inclusion of a broad assortment of Pantheons from all over the world. But would it justify Incan or Polynesian Pantheons, for instance? If Scion <i>doesn\u2019t</i> center its attention on the U.S., what <i>will</i> it use as justification for the various Pantheons interacting? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T19:33:53-08:00","id":74732,"title":"","content":"We South Americans also consume the products of White Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T19:58:49-08:00","id":74738,"title":"","content":"It would seem odd to for an Incan deity to have a scion that was born in Japan. Although in hindsight...lets see...white American with an Egyptian deity father. Ok. Maybe not too odd? Well, justifying the whole of it would simply be part of the creative process for the storyteller I should think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T02:57:55-08:00","id":74860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=74732#post74732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We South Americans also consume the products of White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1st edition Hernan Cortez was a scion of Quetzalcoatl. So why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T05:29:06-08:00","id":74905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=74860#post74860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In 1st edition Hernan Cortez was a scion of Quetzalcoatl. So why not?</div> </div> </div> </div> And he was written as a God. There isn't enough &quot;no&quot; in the universe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T07:02:01-08:00","id":74942,"title":"","content":"Kind of like John Rolfe was a scion of the Algonquin Kabun of the west wind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T12:51:19-08:00","id":75140,"title":"","content":"~~Nadrakas, i thank you for the list. I would like very much,one of the africans panth\u00e9ons you list. But with them, it was the more difficult to choose only ten panth\u00e9ons for the core book. I'm not a fan of the vodoo to, and i prefer the africans Orisha too. The Vodoo is more influenced by christianity. I would not play vodoo gods for that reason in the game and replace them with the Yazata as major panthon. The Orishas i would have play.<br /> I would prefer the great inca pantheon too.<br /> Arghh, only 10 is a very hard choice.<br /> The vodoo is the only one i could possibly remove from my list. And in the same time, i would like too much to see more real africans panth\u00e9ons to add to the Pesedjet.<br /> I could'nt imagine a game about mythology without gaullish or celtic, Greek, Egyptian, Nordic, Japanese, Hindu and Aztec panth\u00e9ons. And a mesopotamian seem very important too, with the importance of the region as the birth of writing and in antiquity. But they are many other great panth\u00e9ons. Inca, Orisha, the many africans you list, that i does'nt know. Ours profs are too bad, lol. I will search about them. For a student in history, with a speciality in antiquity and mythologie, it's a shame to not know them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2307-arcanum-magicae","name":"Arcanum Magicae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T17:27:51-08:00","id":75337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=74328#post74328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brasilian Tupi and Paraguayan Guarani.</div> </div> </div> </div>Failed to mention this earlier, but thank you. We need more of you. Like, ten. People who distinguish between Tupi and Guarani cultures tend to be rare stateside unless you're a cultural anthropologist or an immense Amazonian nerd (I am the latter, dabbled in the former). I blame lack of English sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T05:49:59-08:00","id":75550,"title":"","content":"To be honest, while we know that the Core 6 will be present, I am hoping that the other Pantheons presented in 1e wil get a rewrite for 2e. Failure to do so may leave a lot of groups out in the cold when the Scions they are playing can't be reworked into the new rules. I have a Scion of The Morrigan that I would love to upgrade to 2e, but since the rules are being rebuilt (including PSPs to my knowledge), without a rewrite of the Tuatha Pantheon for 2e, I will either have to rey on &quot;unofficial&quot; conversions or retire her and start over from scratch... something I'd rather not do (how many would like to give up their favorite caracter just because they don't have the rules to convert them?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T07:11:54-08:00","id":75589,"title":"","content":"Yeah; they say that they plan to start out with ten Pantheons in Hero and then add more in subsequent books; for the reasons Shadowstripe indicated, I\u2019m hoping that the initial ten will correlate directly with the ten Pantheons officially published for 1e. They may have different names (e.g., Theoi instead of Dodekatheon, or Teotl instead of Aztlanti) and/or revised concepts (the Loa are reportedly getting an overhaul \u2014 hopefully something tha focuses more on their African roots than on their syncretic diaspora manifestations); but it ought to be recognizably the same ten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T09:38:26-08:00","id":75691,"title":"","content":"The problem overhauling the Loa is the same problem you get separating out the Roman and Greek pantheons. (For that matter, you need to throw in Etruscan and Mycenaen as well. I discount Minoan for the same reason I discount a Gaulish pantheon. We just don't know enough mythology to construct a pantheon. All we got is art. You can have one, but it's going to be largely made up out of whole cloth with very tiny bits if story here and there. As in, less than Pecos Bill, for an explosive example. And the stories about the gods is a core concept to the game.)<br /> <br /> Same for the Celtic pantheons too - Is Manannan mac Lir the same dude as Manawydan fap Llyr? Could be. (Seriously, how could he NOT be.) He just moves to the Isle of Man after he's done with all his shenanigans in the Mabinogien. Is Llew the same as Lugh? Harder sell.<br /> <br /> Do you focus on Voodoo (and, implicitly hoodoo) or do you try to syncretize Voodoun, Staneria, Candomble and Yoruba religion as it's still be practiced? What do you gain and what do you lose? Is it worth it? It's pretty fine-grained to start teasing these guys apart <br /> <br /> I'm interested to see what they do with the &quot;pantheon variance&quot; material in the new game. It's the answer to these questions. But you still have to have something functional in place and that's likely to be a pantheon that does not make these distinctions. Ogun is pretty much Ogun, but Ellegua isn't a whole lot like Legba, But are they close enough together for it to work on a coarse/get more pantheons into the books scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T11:39:41-08:00","id":75779,"title":"","content":"These Pantheons I definitely want to be in he new edition of Scion's corebook....<br /> <br /> Greek (With alternate write-ups for the Roman Pantheon in the next sourcebook)<br /> Egyptian<br /> Norse<br /> Japanese<br /> Hindu<br /> Chinese<br /> Irish/Gaelic (With alternate write-ups for the Welsh Pantheon in the next sourcebook)<br /> <br /> <br /> These Pantheons would work best in the next supplement, at least in my opinion<br /> <br /> Voodoo<br /> Slavic<br /> Aztec<br /> Inca<br /> Sioux<br /> Abrahamic (If it can work, that is, seeing as it's only one deity)<br /> Great Old Ones/Lovecraft<br /> <br /> <br /> Another option I'd like to see is for the corebook to have a guideline for creating you own Pantheon.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T15:12:15-08:00","id":75906,"title":"","content":"Every now and then I think of the area that is the UK, and the Goidels, the Brythons, the Picts, and my imagination conjures up so much...magic in what literature exists. I'd love to see the Welsh get written up in high style. I'm too much a realist to expect it however. A nice notation on D\u00e1l Riata would be demanded though if anything about that geographical region does get written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T18:14:56-08:00","id":76003,"title":"","content":"I think we will eventually get the Welsh Pantheon. If not in the first four books, I bet it will show up later. How could it not? There is so much material there. A lot more than some &quot;A List&quot; pantheons have. <br /> <br /> Good luck with a Pictish pantheon. Once again. We've got some rocks with weird writing on them. A lot less than the Gauls. I'd really like to see the development of the pantheons for which we do have material over those where we're going to be stitching together some off hand references in the writings of other cultures, some artifacts and some architecture. Not that I have a problem with these sort of pantheons being written up. Especially if we get some perspective from the authors: Here's how to deconstruct a pantheon that covered multiple cultures into complete pantheons for each constituent culture... Here's some guidance on how to put together a pantheon from some really thin source material and still have it resonate like the other pantheons... Here's how to develop pantheons based on folklore.... Here's how to bring in pantheons from fictional sources and ways to have them integrate with more mythical mythology... Here's how to have your PC's ditch their home pantheons and make up their own... <br /> <br /> I believe we've been told that the pantheons from Scion:Hero are going to be there + 4 more. So Aztec, Voodoun are going to be in (though they may back up a couple steps and make them Orisha).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T18:38:45-08:00","id":76020,"title":"","content":"As much as people hated the idea, I have to admit that I was intrigued by the Atlantean Gods. Yes, they were made from &quot;whole-cloth&quot; but then how could they not be? Still, a place as mythical and legendary as Atlantis begged for a Pantheon of their own.<br /> <br /> One game that I took part in (that unfortunately didn't last long) had the players portraying reincarnations of these long forgotten Gods. Stripped of much of their power, they had to take on the guise of mortal Scions and slowly rebuild their power. We were seeking out the long lost relics of our former lives, stolen and scattered across the world (their true nature and origin all but forgotten) to regain our birthrights (so to speak). We were also being hounded by the Scions of other Gods who were afraid that we would be turned to worship the Titans... and by Titanspawn who feared that we might join with the Gods against them. The game only lasted one winter (by spring things had picked up that most of the players no longer had set scheduels for weekly gaming), but we were close to reaching Demi-God level.<br /> <br /> While real-world myths and legends of ancient gods are a good place to start, there should be room for forgotten gods of legendary and mythic civilizations that have been lost to time. If the Legends of King Arthur are valid enough to create a pantheon, then why not a fictional pantheon of a land like Atlantis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T19:44:36-08:00","id":76048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=76020#post76020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Legends of King Arthur are valid enough to create a pantheon, then why not a fictional pantheon of a land like Atlantis?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Legends of King Arthur do not really have much in the way of a Pantheon by the 1e definition. The majority are just Heroes with a few Demigods thrown in. They might qualify as a Pantheon in the 2e sense, since it seems that the definition in 2e seems to be &quot;collection of stories&quot; instead of &quot;collection of gods&quot;.<br /> <br /> And Atlantis would probably be ruled by the Theoi. But let's not go down that road again =P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T19:48:26-08:00","id":76051,"title":"","content":"There wasn't a Legend of King Arthur pantheon in canon, though -- and honestly, pantheons based off of folklore rather than mythology tend to be a little haphazard, whether sourcebook or fanon. A guide to creating fictional pantheons might be a good place to include the Atlantean one, though, in a step by step example process.<br /> <br /> To be honest, though, I think myths and legends make better terra incognita than pantheons. Visiting an Atlantis created by a student of Plato who happened to be a scion of Jupiter or Neptune, trying to get back to his more Grecian roots by bringing this &quot;greek myth&quot; to life? Could be fascinating, especially given how quickly utopias tend to fall . . . and visiting El Dorado! Yes *w* Visiting the ruins of Camelot and reviving Arthur to fight for the gods. Or even going so far as borrowing from history to make a ghost ship of the Titanic, or an immortalized Pompeii.<br /> <br /> This isn't the thread for terra incognita though, so I'll buzz off now. Aaah, I wonder if anyone's posted their fanmade terra incognita at all *w* and is it incognita or incognitae. . .?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T06:55:27-08:00","id":76250,"title":"","content":"Since it's an adjective modifying &quot;terra&quot; it would be &quot;terrae incognitae&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T07:06:03-08:00","id":76256,"title":"","content":"If you dig back into the old stuff, the original King Arthur material (like Culhwch &amp; Olwen old) is patently an example of Celtic Heroes (and a smattering of Demigods) running around. Most probably associated with what we would call the Welsh pantheon. It's just an example of a pantheon with a robust narrative at the Hero level. Like the Greek, Irish, Chinese, etc. <br /> <br /> Which, to my thinking, means it would be ideal stuff for pantheons slated to go into Hero. Some mythologies are all about the Gods (and Demigods). Good examples of what mythological/legendary heroes actually DO. <br /> <br /> Too bad that Welsh and Irish are so close as to be intertwined in an area already rich in equally and more familiar pantheons. One or the other until later (maybe some teasers, like they did when they said Mannana mac Llyr was was an outsider to the Tuatha De and they mentioned how they were &quot;borrowing&quot; the Annwyn from the Welsh).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T07:10:14-08:00","id":76257,"title":"","content":"Oh, and last one, since I got to get ready to PLAY Scion... If the original Atlantis source material is Plato, a Greek. Plato's mouthpiece Critias out and out says that Atlantis belongs to Poseidon, what's the argument about it being Hellenistic? Besides the made up stuff from Demigod. Add in the fact that the real template for the myth is Santorini and a Minoan (pre-Hellenistic) civilization. Atlantis seems like a lock for the premiere Terra Incognita for the Theoi. Especially since they described it a bit more than the other really good ones, like Hyperborea, etc. <br /> <br /> It's relevant to the thread, to me, because a good example Terra (or two or three)should be a part of every pantheon description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T09:16:21-08:00","id":76325,"title":"","content":"For me, I want to see the Babylonian pantheon, and I want to see some more modern pantheons too. Sure, not everyone liked the Allied Pantheon, but you know what? If the rules are going to allow PCs to design their own pantheons, I'm pretty sure they wouldn't have been the first ones to do it. I actually made a pantheon for my campaign which 'absorbed' gods from other pantheons, and created a pantheon which catered to more modern concepts. We had a goddess of the media, a god of the internet, and so forth, all designed around the modern era. IIRC&lt; I called it the Network, I'll need to check my old notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T10:00:14-08:00","id":76363,"title":"","content":"Would it be too weird to have a Titan Pantheon? One with Prometheus &amp; Hyperion?<br /> <br /> I think there should be unaligned gods too. Like Santa Clause. Any god that doesn't quite fit into any other Pantheon but is still popular/ powerful enough not to be forgotten","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:33:42-08:00","id":76450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aermas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=76363#post76363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be too weird to have a Titan Pantheon? One with Prometheus &amp; Hyperion?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the writers has mentioned children of figures who'd likely be considered Titans in 1e, like Nyx and Chronos. What they'll be in 2e... no clue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=74726#post74726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Although it brings up an interesting question: where will the default Scion settings focus their attention? Traditionally, White Wolf has focused on the people inhabiting North America in general, and the United States in particular; given the nation\u2019s \u201cmelting pot\u201d nature, that leaves a lot of room to justify the inclusion of a broad assortment of Pantheons from all over the world. But would it justify Incan or Polynesian Pantheons, for instance? If Scion <i>doesn\u2019t</i> center its attention on the U.S., what <i>will</i> it use as justification for the various Pantheons interacting?</div> </div> </div> </div>A thought that occurred to me was that the settings wouldn't be geographically focused, as with the Worlds of Darkness; instead, they'd be more like Exalted's Shards, worlds with differing base assumptions (like whether or not there's a Masquerade, or whether or not the gods ever withdrew to the Firmament). A world where the existence of the gods and Scions has never been forgotten is very different from one where the gods have only recently returned, and have as yet not announced themselves publicly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T17:21:23-08:00","id":76718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Magicae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=75140#post75140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~~Nadrakas, i thank you for the list. I would like very much,one of the africans panth\u00e9ons you list. But with them, it was the more difficult to choose only ten panth\u00e9ons for the core book. I'm not a fan of the vodoo to, and i prefer the africans Orisha too. The Vodoo is more influenced by christianity. I would not play vodoo gods for that reason in the game and replace them with the Yazata as major panthon. The Orishas i would have play.<br /> I would prefer the great inca pantheon too.<br /> Arghh, only 10 is a very hard choice.<br /> The vodoo is the only one i could possibly remove from my list. And in the same time, i would like too much to see more real africans panth\u00e9ons to add to the Pesedjet.<br /> I could'nt imagine a game about mythology without gaullish or celtic, Greek, Egyptian, Nordic, Japanese, Hindu and Aztec panth\u00e9ons. And a mesopotamian seem very important too, with the importance of the region as the birth of writing and in antiquity. But they are many other great panth\u00e9ons. Inca, Orisha, the many africans you list, that i does'nt know. Ours profs are too bad, lol. I will search about them. For a student in history, with a speciality in antiquity and mythologie, it's a shame to not know them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcanum Magicae,<br /> <br /> You are very welcome. I think that the African Pantheons are very important <i>(They all are, in their own way)</i>. Not everything can be fit into the main book, and any attempt to create a &quot;Book of Pantheons&quot; would result in a multi-volume creation. Fortunately, we have the Scion Community that can pick up where the Devs have to leave off <i>(Not picking on the Devs. Some Very hard decisions have to be made, and I understand and fully support that. Heck...new Pantheons can be added later)</i>.<br /> <br /> I for one intend to add non-traditional Pantheons pulled from the imaginations of the Human Populous into my game with 1e <i>(I know this won't win me too many fans...but what the heck...).</i> I did this in my own Scion game, and it added some depth and breadth to the game <i>(They weren't a &quot;big&quot; factor -- not on stage, all the time...but they showcased a growing world to the players...)</i>. <br /> <br /> <br /> Some ideas <i>(Not asking them to be developed &quot;Officially,&quot; mind you)</i>:<br /> <br /> The &quot;Holiday&quot; spirits:<br /> - Father Christmas (Olde Style, replete with a Sword. Defender of Children, Protector of the Innocent)<br /> - The Spirit of Easter (Renewal, rebirth, healing)<br /> - The Hallowed Lady (Protector of the Dead, Avenger of Martyrs, Guide of Hallows)<br /> - The Married Couple (Protectors of Marriage, Mother's, Fathers)<br /> - Mother of Spring (Patron of Groves, Bringer of Spring, Birth)<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>(And others...)</i> -- most of these are very specific, of limited scope, or a cover a limited period of time. They didn't play a big part in the game, but were cool for background flavor, and showed the players that &quot;Hey...there are other thing's going on besides the 'Big Guys, from before.'&quot; <br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T19:24:23-08:00","id":76802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=76250#post76250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it's an adjective modifying &quot;terra&quot; it would be &quot;terrae incognitae&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was close. Thank you! :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and last one, since I got to get ready to PLAY Scion... If the original Atlantis source material is Plato, a Greek. Plato's mouthpiece Critias out and out says that Atlantis belongs to Poseidon, what's the argument about it being Hellenistic? Besides the made up stuff from Demigod. Add in the fact that the real template for the myth is Santorini and a Minoan (pre-Hellenistic) civilization. Atlantis seems like a lock for the premiere Terra Incognita for the Theoi. Especially since they described it a bit more than the other really good ones, like Hyperborea, etc.<br /> <br /> It's relevant to the thread, to me, because a good example Terra (or two or three)should be a part of every pantheon description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, having a terra incognita (or a few) for each pantheon presented in the core book(s) would be amazing.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also kind of like the idea of systems for gods that are more standalone/don't have the backing for a pantheon. For instance, if a scion ascended to god, and rejected their pantheon, but didn't create a new one, what would happen?<br /> <br /> But as for the pantheons presented in Hero, I'd like for the ten to be the ones already presented in 1e. Like has been said, being able to update old characters to the new edition is something that should be kept in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T06:21:31-08:00","id":77622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=76802#post76802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also kind of like the idea of systems for gods that are more standalone/don't have the backing for a pantheon. For instance, if a scion ascended to god, and rejected their pantheon, but didn't create a new one, what would happen?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under normal circumstances such a god would be exceedingly likely to end up dead. But since this is a PC, if they manage to avoid all the pitfalls that would result in their grizzly demise, then they would either:<br /> <br /> <b>A)</b> Still be a member of their pantheon, and retain their PSP, while simply removing themselves from social interactions with their pantheon.<br /> <b>B)</b> Undergo some dramatic fate effect that would genuinely remove them from their pantheon, and strip them of their PSP.<br /> <b>C)</b> Undergo some dramatic fate effect that would genuinely remove them from their pantheon, and keep their PSP because their storyteller took pity on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T13:58:22-08:00","id":77813,"title":"","content":"When they came up with the Irish and Persian Pantheons most of my wishes were granted. That said. the Orishas would be fun. Exploring the Indonesian pantheons got absorbed by the Devas and strive to preserve their identity by promoting Buddhist ideals would be grand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T23:28:10-08:00","id":80041,"title":"","content":"The Core 6 and the pantheons listed in the Companion seem to be the main runners. Runner ups seem to be the Native American pantheon, being that Coyote is shown talking with Yukiko in Scion: God's fiction, not to mention the Mesopotamian pantheon noted in the Pesdajet part of the book's adventure where Horace had to figure out who was Aten's suicide bomber. And real or not, the Atlantis pantheon was considered canon in the Scion game universe when they were written up for Demigod, so seeing them again will keep up with the spirit of the term Urban Fantasy (since Atlantis is considered by most a fantasy).<br /> <br /> Another pantheon that I think should get written in is the Cannite pantheon (the pantheon that's the precursor for the arrival of the Yahweh cult (since according to historians, Jews originally called Yahweh, &quot;El&quot;. The reason why I want this so bad is that I find it disturbing that Christian fundamentalists aren't losing their minds (in the game world) when Scions and those Fatebound to them claim that the god or goddess that the Abrahamic religions demonized are more real than God. I would be thinking that Baptists in Florida would conduct protest and smear campaigns to suppress the pantheons and their Scions. Hell, they have been doing that for over a millenia and they still do (as a counterpoint to paganists who worship the old gods.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T02:19:57-08:00","id":80125,"title":"","content":"While I\u2019m in favor of there being <i>something</i> in the setting to support the notion that worshippers of the Abrahamic faiths aren\u2019t <i>utterly</i> delusional (i.e., simultaneously denying the existence of gods that absolutely <i>do</i> exist in the setting while worshipping a God that <i>doesn\u2019t</i> exist in the setting), I don\u2019t think that the Elohim should be included for that purpose. If they\u2019re included, it should be because said Pantheon\u2019s mythology is interesting in its own right. <br /> <br /> All that said, I wouldn\u2019t mind the Loa being replaced by the the Orishas in <b>Scion: Hero</b>, with the Voodoo Pantheon specifically being held back for later inclustion in a post-<b>Scion: God</b> supplement devoted to Pantheons and the like that are connected in some way or another to the Abrahamic faiths: the Canaanite Pantheon that Abraham\u2019s God waged war against, the Arabian Pantheon whose human followers were nearly wiped out by the rise of Islam, the Carribean religions that syncretized African and Christian beliefs, and so on: in short, all of the Pantheons that get awkward to talk about without referencing Abrahamic faiths. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d also like to see the order of introduction of Pantheons reflect the books involved: <b>Scion: Hero</b> should feature Pantheons that are either still actively worshipped today (e.g., Indian and Japanese Pantheons) or that have a significant presence in popular culture (e.g., Greek, Norse, and Egyptian Pantheons), while <b>Scion: God</b> should introduce Pantheons of more ancient pedigree who no longer involve themselves all that much with the current affairs of the World but are still significant presences in the Overworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T06:01:12-08:00","id":80183,"title":"","content":"Como E Imposs\u00edvel ter hum MESMO Livro de Todos os pante\u00f5es Relevantes. Alguem poderia Pensar Que hum Programa de Expans\u00e3o par\u00e1grafo CRIAR UM Livro POR Continente. Os livros dos continentes pode incluir pelo menos um pante\u00e3o Cada regi\u00e3o que existe neste continente visto no mapa. Considering geologicamente e historicamente as antes da chegada dos europeus \u00e0 Am\u00e9rica do Sul. E hum Continente \u00e0 parte). Mapa <a href=\"http://metalgaia.files.wordpress.com/2013/06/964390_329719203820336_925162630_o.jpg?w=590\" target=\"_blank\">http://metalgaia.files.wordpress.com...30_o.jpg?w=590</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","user":"Ben Linus","date":". 02-26-2014, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:30:09-08:00","id":80293,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Orishas in Hero and the Loa in whatever book they tell us how to divide pantheons up by constituent culture (a la Graeco-Roman into Graeco and Roman). So Orisha into Loa, Orisha, etc. <br /> <br /> I'll miss the good Baron though. A lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:55:17-08:00","id":80315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=80183#post80183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Como E Imposs\u00edvel ter hum MESMO Livro de Todos os pante\u00f5es Relevantes. Alguem poderia Pensar Que hum Programa de Expans\u00e3o par\u00e1grafo CRIAR UM Livro POR Continente. Os livros dos continentes pode incluir pelo menos um pante\u00e3o Cada regi\u00e3o que existe neste continente visto no mapa. Considering geologicamente e historicamente as antes da chegada dos europeus \u00e0 Am\u00e9rica do Sul. E hum Continente \u00e0 parte). Mapa <a href=\"http://metalgaia.files.wordpress.com/2013/06/964390_329719203820336_925162630_o.jpg?w=590\" target=\"_blank\">http://metalgaia.files.wordpress.com...30_o.jpg?w=590</a></div> </div> </div> </div>(Thank goodness for Google Translate\u2026) If I read this correctly, I tend to agree: a series of regional books, each featuring up to, say, a half-dozen Pantheons originating from that region, would be a nice way to go. I wouldn\u2019t necessarily go by Continent; there\u2019s enough going on in and around the Middle East region alone to easily support half a dozen Pantheons, to say nothing of Eastern Europe/Western Asia, or the various island nations off the coast of Southeast Asia; trying to lump everything from Russia to China to Indonesia to the Arabian Peninsula in one book would be a bit much. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:32:06-08:00","id":80390,"title":"","content":"Re: the Companion pantheons, there's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=898#post898\">this comment</a> from Neall. Make of it what you will:<br /> <br /> <i>I will say that the additional (new, rather than Companion) pantheons we're batting around for inclusion are all over the globe in terms of locations. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T20:41:40-08:00","id":81394,"title":"","content":"A Celtic pantheon, not necessary Tuatha D\u00e9 Dannan or Nementondevos, it could be more general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2400-nightbird","user":"Nightbird","date":". 02-27-2014, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2400-nightbird","name":"Nightbird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2400_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T08:51:44-08:00","id":81612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightbird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/73035-what-pantheon-would-you-like-to-see?p=81394#post81394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Celtic pantheon, not necessary Tuatha D\u00e9 Dannan or Nementondevos, it could be more general.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be... difficult. Some deities are similar across pantheons. Some are very much not so.... Lugh v. Llew (v. Lug, maybe, very little info to go on), Nuada v. Nyth v. Nodens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T10:03:47-08:00","id":82143,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind seeing something beyond the Egyptians coming out of Africa. <br /> <br /> I would also like to see a few more of the gods added to the pantheons that are already there (Sekmet for example from Egypt). Though you'd have to tread carefully not to double up on a pantheon's gods if your trying not to invalidate one god or another, an example being if they added Thanatos to the Dodekatheon, since he is actually the god of Death there, not Hades, but the book and folks in general tend to associate Hades with Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}